      "message": "too long for a subject.\n\nalso, start with a lowercase verb. Look at the git log for examples, or see https://golang.org/doc/contribute.html and search for \"should complete the sentence\" on that page:\n\nThe first line of the change description is conventionally a one-line summary of the change, prefixed by the primary affected package, and is used as the subject for code review email. It should complete the sentence \"This change modifies Go to _____.\" The rest of the description elaborates and should provide context for the change and explain what it does. Write in complete sentences with correct punctuation, just like for your comments in Go. If there is a helpful reference, mention it here. If you\u0027ve fixed an issue, reference it by number with a # before it.",
